§ `s 8C(2)`

-- k020: Jake at 15, with no job, has not quoted his TFN to anyone: that alone is not a failure to give information.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I taken to have failed to give information` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I taken to have failed to give information` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 8WA, 8WB`

-- c020: the TFN declaration is treated as provided for by a taxation law (INFERENCE: the provision is ITAA 1936 Part VA,
-- not read). A video store asking for a TFN as identification commits the offence. Jake's agent acts on his behalf.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it an offence to ask me for my TFN` `c020: the supermarket asks Chloe for her TFN on a TFN declaration`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to ask me for my TFN` `a video store asks for a TFN as proof of identity`
#ASSERT NOT `Is it an offence to ask me for my TFN` `k043: Jake's tax agent asks for his TFN to lodge his return`

#ASSERT `Is it an offence to record, use or pass on my TFN` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 12-1, 12-10, 12-35, 12-190`

-- c020, d012, c041: wages must have tax withheld whatever the employee's age and whether or not a TFN was quoted.
-- k043: a business paying Jake for deliveries withholds nothing once his ABN is on the invoice; it must withhold from $400
-- with no ABN quoted, but not from $50 (not more than $50).
#ASSERT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `c020: Chloe's casual wages from the supermarket at 15`
#ASSERT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `d012: Daniel's casual wages at 16, no TFN quoted yet`
#ASSERT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `c041: Chloe's February 2024 salary of 5833.33`
#ASSERT NOT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `a non-cash benefit given to an employee`
#ASSERT NOT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `k043: a business pays Jake 400 for deliveries, his ABN on the invoice`
#ASSERT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `k043: a business pays Jake 400, no ABN quoted`
#ASSERT NOT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `k043: a business pays Jake 50, no ABN quoted`
#ASSERT NOT `Must tax be withheld from my payment` `a business pays 400 to a hobbyist who gave a hobby statement`

§ `Regulations ss 5, 26, 38`

-- k043: the top rate is 45% + 2% = 47%. 400 x 47% = 188. A payment of 333.50 is rounded to 333; 333 x 47% = 156.51,
-- rounded to 156.
#ASSERT `How much is withheld when I quote no ABN` 400 EQUALS 188
#ASSERT `How much is withheld when I quote no ABN` 333.50 EQUALS 156

§ `ss 15-10, 15-15, 16-20, 16-30`

-- c041: the schedule amount is an input; 1000 is HYPOTHETICAL (the schedules are not deposited). Once withheld, her
-- employer owes her nothing more for it; had it not withheld, it would owe the Commissioner a penalty of the same 1000.
#ASSERT `How much must be withheld from my wages` 1000 FALSE 0 EQUALS 1000

#ASSERT NOT `Can my payer still be made to pay me what it withheld` TRUE

#ASSERT `What does my payer owe for not withholding` 1000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1000

§ `ss 16-75, 16-95, 16-100, 16-105`

-- c041: Chloe's employer's size is not in the scenario. HYPOTHETICAL: 30,000 withheld last year makes it medium; exactly
-- 25,000 does not ("exceeded"). Her February 2024 tax is due to the Commissioner on 21 March 2024 (medium) or 21 April 2024
-- (small). A deferred BAS medium withholder's December amount is due on 28 February.
#ASSERT `What size of withholder is my payer` 30000 30000 2500 EQUALS `a medium withholder`
#ASSERT `What size of withholder is my payer` 25000 25000 2000 EQUALS `a small withholder`

#ASSERT `By when must my payer pay over what it withheld` `a medium withholder` (Date 29 2 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 21 3 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must my payer pay over what it withheld` `a small withholder` (Date 29 2 2024) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 21 4 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must my payer pay over what it withheld` `a medium withholder` (Date 15 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)

§ `ss 16-155, 389-20`

-- c041: reported through single touch payroll, so no payment summary is owed. d012: if Daniel's 2012-13 wages were not so
-- reported (HYPOTHETICAL, and on the 2026 text), by 14 July 2013.
#ASSERT `By when must I be given a payment summary` TRUE TRUE 2024 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I be given a payment summary` TRUE FALSE 2013 EQUALS JUST (Date 14 7 2013)

§ `Regulations s 56`

-- A worker who claimed the tax-free threshold and then becomes a foreign resident must give a new declaration.
#ASSERT `Must I give a new declaration` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

§ `s 18-15`

-- c041: on assessment, a credit for the whole of what was withheld in the year (9,000, HYPOTHETICAL).
#ASSERT `What credit do I get for tax withheld` 9000 TRUE EQUALS 9000

